{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they rose up before Moses.</b> Korah disputed because he was the firstborn of his father's sons and the greatness was given to Aaron; and Dathan and Abiram and On — because the birthright was taken from Reuben their father and given to Joseph, for they thought that on account of Joshua, who was his minister and was from the tribe of Joseph, he did so. And 'princes of the congregation' — because they were firstborns. And a proof for the matter: at the blossoming of the staff it says ותכל תלונותם, for they saw that the staff of Levi was chosen in place of the firstborns. And further, as it is written: כי כל העדה כלם קדושים — an allusion to the firstborns, as it is written of them: קדש לי כל בכור." "<b>And men of the children of Israel, two hundred and fifty.</b> He took for himself twenty-three from every tribe, besides the tribe of Levi, from whom the grievance came, so that from every tribe there would be a minor Sanhedrin; in total together with On, Dathan, and Abiram — two hundred and fifty and three. Here Rashi explained: he dressed them in mantles that were entirely tekhelet. One may say: because HaShem commanded above, immediately beforehand, the commandment of tzitzit, Korah came against Moses over this commandment." "<b>Called ones of the appointed time.</b> For they were called to the Tent of Meeting."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:13.379143435Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}